# Safe handling of external / shared repos

Before cloning, installing dependencies, building Docker from an unknown Dockerfile, or running scripts from a third-party or “shared” repo (including job practical tests, HR links, random GitHub repos):

1. Inspect the repo first (README, install scripts, package hooks, obfuscated code, unexpected network/credential access).
2. Tell the user what looks safe vs risky.
3. Wait for explicit user approval before clone/install/run.

Prefer reading docs or building from scratch over executing untrusted code.

“Job test” or “practical assignment” repos are **not** automatically safe.
